# --- Saturn build output -----------------------------------------------------
saturn/BuildDrop/
**/*.o
**/*.elf
**/*.iso
**/*.cue
**/*.bin.tmp
# 0.bin is the linked program objcopy'd into the disc image on every build.
# It is committed as part of the CD skeleton, so ignore only the build dir above.

# --- Cross-compiler and iso2raw (fetched into the SDK submodule, never committed)
SaturnRingLib/Compiler/
SaturnRingLib/tools/bin/

# --- Host/IDE build dirs -----------------------------------------------------
cmake-build-*/

# --- Non-free game data ------------------------------------------------------
# Another World's original PC DOS data files. Required to run, never committed.
# Both cases listed: the engine asks for them lowercase (bank.cxx builds the name
# with sprintf("bank%02x")) and ISO9660 stores them uppercase, so either spelling
# can show up on disk depending on where they were copied from. Git's ignore
# matching is case-sensitive wherever core.ignorecase is false, e.g. CI on Linux.
saturn/cd/data/BANK*
saturn/cd/data/bank*
saturn/cd/data/MEMLIST.BIN
saturn/cd/data/memlist.bin
